[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known as one issue. It is two. Of the 412 unique
reports merged into it, the table below counts them by tenant and booking form.

<Callout>
Closed 5 October: the parser problem is fixed; the form hint problem will not be fixed.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

1. **Parser, 379 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is the bug #4471 describes. **Fixed**: parse dd/mm for eu locales. Five of these read as a one-day move (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620); the desk counts them here, by tenant.
2. **Form hint, 33 reports.** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People on day-first tenants type month first, and the form reads it their way. Intake tagged these `parser`; the tenant and form say otherwise. **Won't fix**: the `booking-v3` form was retired.

## Why the merge hid this

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. These reports share
subjects such as "Wrong day on the invite" while their causes differ. The export also repeats 15 report
ids; count each id once.

## Tickets

One GitHub issue per problem, in `Lstanislao/what-it-shows-s01e03`: #1 parser (379 reports), #2 form hint (33 reports).

